    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Sam Antonacci** leading the charge as our strongest play. With a score of 63.61, **Sam Antonacci** benefits from a prime leadoff spot against Rocker, whose 4.36 xERA provides a favorable environment for **Sam Antonacci** to capitalize on his elite speed and high-OBP skill set. While **Nasim Nunez** (59.76) slots in lower due to his position at the bottom of the order, he remains a highly recommended start; the matchup against Feltner (5.10 xERA) is one of the softest on the board, and his high sprint speed remains a critical asset in our pursuit of category gains in SB. **Miguel Vargas** (55.00) rounds out the infield, maintaining a solid floor thanks to his role in the #3 hole, despite a neutral matchup against Rocker.\n\nThe most difficult decision today involves **Jackson Merrill**, who sits at 51.66. While **Jackson Merrill** faces a tougher test against the 3.28 xERA of Ashcraft, he retains value due to a dynamic platoon advantage and a projected middle-of-the-order presence. His score is effectively tethered to the \"Lineup Pending\" status; if he drops in the order, his utility diminishes, but for now, his upside warrants the start over our deep bench. We remain cautious regarding the heavy hitters sitting out, as the absence of **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** due to scheduling gaps forces us to lean on the efficiency of our fringe starters. We are effectively managing our daily game caps by shielding stars like **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** from today\u2019s specific pitcher matchups, ensuring they are fresh for higher-scoring windows later in the week.",
